{"key": "7951", "mpkey": "2094", "stat": "A", "schd": "A", "code": "PSY 340", "section": "001", "crn": "12186", "title": "COGNITIVE PSYCHOLOGY", "session_html": "Full Term (11 week; Fall/Winter/Spring/Summer) (09-23-2026 to 12-04-2026)", "hours_html": "4", "rpt_for_credit": "", "campus": "Oregon State - Corvallis", "sche_type_clss_fild": "Lecture", "inst_mthd": "In-Person Section", "grade_mode": "Normal Grading Mode", "status": "Open", "max_enroll": "75", "enrollment": "74", "ssbsect_seats_avail": "1", "waitlist_capacity": "8", "ssbsect_wait_count": "0", "ssbsect_wait_avail": "8", "cross_list_max_enroll": "", "xlist_wait_cap": "", "ssbxlst_seats_avail": "", "description": "Provides an in-depth analysis of a variety of topics related to cognitive psychology introduced in lower-division coursework. Explores the processes involved in the creation and storage of mental representations of objects, situations, actions and states, and the use of these representations to guide behavior. Emphasizes critical evaluation of empirical research and theoretical models beyond the introductory level. Covers topics including perception, attention, memory, reasoning, decision making, and language.", "registration_restrictions": "<p class=\"prereq\">Prerequisites: <a href=\"/search/?p=PSY%20201\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:PSY 201\" >PSY 201</a>, <a href=\"/search/?p=PSY%20201H\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:PSY 201H\"  class=\"notoffered\">201H</a>, <a href=\"/search/?p=PSY%20201Z\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:PSY 201Z\" >201Z</a> or 201HZ.<br/>A minimum grade of C- is required in <a href=\"/search/?p=PSY%20201\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:PSY 201\" >PSY 201</a>, <a href=\"/search/?p=PSY%20201H\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:PSY 201H\"  class=\"notoffered\">PSY 201H</a>, <a href=\"/search/?p=PSY%20201Z\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:PSY 201Z\" >PSY 201Z</a> and <a hre